## Phase 1: Storage Diagnostics & Auditing

### 1.1 Check Current Drive Utilization
```cmd
powershell -Command "Get-PSDrive C | Select-Object @{N='Used(GB)';E={[math]::Round($_.Used/1GB,2)}}, @{N='Free(GB)';E={[math]::Round($_.Free/1GB,2)}}"
```

### 1.2 Export Installed Applications Report (OneDrive-Safe Path)
Exports all registry-tracked applications sorted by size to your actual Desktop path (works even when OneDrive Folder Backup is enabled).
```cmd
powershell -Command "Get-ItemProperty HKLM:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\*, HKLM:\Software\Wow6432Node\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\*, HKCU:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\* -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.DisplayName } | Select-Object DisplayName, @{Name='Size(MB)';Expression={[math]::Round($_.EstimatedSize / 1024, 2)}} | Sort-Object 'Size(MB)' -Descending | Format-Table -AutoSize | Out-File ([Environment]::GetFolderPath('Desktop') + '\AppsReport.txt')"
```

### 1.3 Audit Windows Volume Shadow Copies (System Restore)
Verify whether Windows' native System Restore is consuming hidden space:
```cmd
vssadmin list shadowstorage
```

### 1.4 Inspect Hidden Root Files (`hiberfil.sys` / `pagefile.sys`)
```cmd
dir /a C:\
```

### 1.5 Scan Top 15 Largest `AppData` Directories
```cmd
powershell -Command "Get-ChildItem $env:LOCALAPPDATA, $env:APPDATA -Directory -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { $s = (Get-ChildItem $_.FullName -Recurse -Force -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object Length -Sum).Sum; [PSCustomObject]@{ Folder = $_.FullName; 'Size(GB)' = [math]::Round($s / 1GB, 2) } } | Sort-Object 'Size(GB)' -Descending | Select-Object -First 15 | Format-Table -AutoSize"
```

### 1.6 Scan Top 15 System & Program Directories
*(Note: `C:\Users\All Users` is a system junction pointing to `C:\ProgramData`—do not count or delete it separately.)*
```cmd
powershell -Command "Get-ChildItem 'C:\ProgramData','C:\Program Files','C:\Program Files (x86)','C:\Windows','C:\Users' -Directory -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Where-Object { $_.FullName -ne $env:USERPROFILE } | ForEach-Object { $s = (Get-ChildItem $_.FullName -Recurse -Force -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object Length -Sum).Sum; [PSCustomObject]@{ Folder = $_.FullName; 'Size(GB)' = [math]::Round($s / 1GB, 2) } } | Sort-Object 'Size(GB)' -Descending | Select-Object -First 15 | Format-Table -AutoSize"
```

