## Phase 5: Real-Time CLI Monitoring (Linux `watch` / `mpstat` / `htop` Equivalents)

* **Live Disk & Process Monitor (`watch -n 2` equivalent):**
  ```cmd
  powershell -Command "while($true){ cls; Get-PSDrive C | Select-Object @{N='Used(GB)';E={[math]::Round($_.Used/1GB,2)}}, @{N='Free(GB)';E={[math]::Round($_.Free/1GB,2)}}; Get-Process robocopy -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name, Id, @{N='RAM(MB)';E={[math]::Round($_.WS/1MB,1)}}; Start-Sleep 2 }"
  ```
* **Live CPU, RAM, & Disk Telemetry (`mpstat` equivalent):**
  ```cmd
  typeperf "\Processor(_Total)\% Processor Time" "\Memory\% Committed Bytes In Use" "\LogicalDisk(C:)\% Disk Time" "\LogicalDisk(C:)\Free Megabytes" -si 2
  ```
* **Interactive Terminal Dashboard (`htop` equivalent):**
  ```cmd
  winget install aristocratos.btop4win
  btop
  ```

